   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What they say",
     "texto": [
      "**-대요** is the colloquial contracted form for quoting a statement: 가다 → **간대요** (they say (he/she) is going), 먹다 → **먹는대요** (they say (he/she) eats), 피곤하다 → **피곤하대요** (they say (he/she) is tired), 학생이다 → **학생이래요** (they say (he/she) is a student). Depending on the context, it means «they say that…» or «I've been told that…»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Difference from -다고 하다",
     "texto": [
      "**-다고 해요** is the affirmative quote without contraction; **-대요** is the contracted form, common in conversation. Both convey a statement attributed to another source: they are not simply distinguished as «what someone said» versus «a rumour»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
